From a0ad63701b232141603f92b02f149f1c4658c7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sreeram S <sreeram@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:37:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: repair a blank Home after a quick power off and on
 (Realtek ASU, Sony BRAVIA VU2)

The tuner's Automatic Service Update (com.realtek.dtv ASUService) opens its
Digital Channel Setup screen at every power-off. A power-on within a second or
two then restarts and resumes Home while its window is still invisible:

- the refocus in reloadApps finds no laid-out tile, and the glass/hero fades it
  starts stay at alpha 0 while the flags say shown;
- the process can miss the display's ON event, after which every window in it
  skips each draw (mLastPerformDrawFailedReason=screen_off), so recreate() does
  not help and only a new process does.

After each screen-on and window focus, Home now asks for one draw. If nothing
is drawn while PowerManager.isInteractive(), it restarts its process (at most
once a minute, logged as TvHome; Android relaunches the top Home). Otherwise it
repairs stuck tiles and fades through the existing refocus path.

Tested on a BRAVIA VU2 (UKR1.240726.001): quick power cycles, an app round
trip, and quick power cycles after a restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JNks2QG6pJ57GLCSB3q7K5
