 examples/sony-bravia-vu2/debloat.txt          |  3 +
 .../java/com/gathin/tvhome/MainActivity.java  | 92 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 109 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md b/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md
index c6f4c193..d272a8c7 100644
--- a/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md
+++ b/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md
@@ -782,6 +782,20 @@ Things that bit us or contributors, so they don't bite you. Commands use `tools/
   `.RecoveryActivity` on a Xiaomi MiTV-MOEU0 (`V816.0.26.10.12.1`), `set-home-activity` did not change it,
   and after one reboot the TV never left the boot animation and only a factory reset brought it back
   ([#3578](https://github.com/Gathin23/cleanyourtv/issues/3578)). Enable launcherx first, every time.
+- **Home comes back with no tiles, highlight or name after a quick power off and on** (Sony BRAVIA VU2,
+  Realtek `rtd2885m`, Android 14 `UKR1.240726.001`). The top bar and the empty dock band show; one arrow key
+  brings the tiles back but not the glass or the app name, and only a force-stop of `com.gathin.tvhome` brings
+  everything back. The tuner's Automatic Service Update (`com.realtek.dtv` `ASUService`) opens
+  `.DigitalSetup.DigitalChannelSetupActivity` at every power-off, so a power-on within a second or two restarts
+  and resumes Home while its window is still invisible behind that screen. Two things go wrong: the refocus in
+  `reloadApps` finds no laid-out tile and the fades it starts stay at alpha 0, and the launcher process can miss
+  the display's ON event, after which every window in it skips each draw
+  (`tools/tv.py "dumpsys activity top" | grep mLastPerformDrawFailedReason` says `screen_off` while the window is
+  focused and visible, `dumpsys gfxinfo com.gathin.tvhome` stops counting frames, the clock stops). `recreate()`
+  does not help, since the stale display state belongs to the process. The launcher now checks after each
+  screen-on and window focus that Home draws: if nothing is drawn while `PowerManager.isInteractive()`, it
+  restarts its process (once a minute at most, logged as `TvHome`), and otherwise repairs stuck fades and tiles.
+  Turning Automatic Service Update off avoids the trigger; the tuner itself must stay enabled.
 - **Home worked for days, then went black after a power cut** (Acer R4G and Panasonic 4KTV-3MUP,
   MOKA `R4_GTV`, Google TV 14): the firmware re-enables setupwraith at every cold boot and its
   `.RecoveryActivity` takes Home. `logcat | grep RecoveryActivity` shows it starting several times a
diff --git a/examples/sony-bravia-vu2/debloat.txt b/examples/sony-bravia-vu2/debloat.txt
